    "https://jobs.roosevelt.edu:443/postings/8877": {
      "title": "Roosevelt University Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Roosevelt University Employment Opportunities | Payroll Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help New Users Returning Users Payroll Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Payroll Manager Category Administrative Position Number Posting Number S0001391 Location Hybrid - Chicago Open Date 09/03/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? No Job Type Full-Time Working Hours Position Summary The Payroll Manager leads payroll operations and ensures accurate, timely, and compliant processing of the University’s biweekly and monthly payrolls. This role oversees payroll processing, tax reporting, reconciliations, systems, audits, and employee support while partnering with HR, Finance, Financial Aid, and departments to improve controls, processes, and service. The Payroll Manager reports to the Associate Vice President of HR Technology & Solutions. This is a full-time, at-will, exempt position. The position is full-time, hybrid, and requires the employee to report to the Chicago campus 3 days per week. The hours are Monday–Friday, 8:30AM.–5:00PM. Occasional additional hours may be required during payroll processing, year-end processing, audits, or other critical payroll deadlines. Roosevelt University offers many great benefits. Please review our benefits in further detail by clicking this link: https://rooseveltu.touchpointsonline.com/ The salary range for this position is $70,000-$75,000 Title IX Contact Information: Federal Title IX policy requires that all colleges and universities make known the contact information for the person responsible for coordinating its efforts to comply with Title IX regulations. At Roosevelt University, the Title IX Coordinator is Natasha Robinson. Her office is located in the Auditorium Building of the Chicago campus, 430 S. Michigan Avenue, AUD 476B. She can be reached at 312-281-3245 or TitleIX@roosevelt.edu. Do not contact this email address for inquiries about your job application; if you have questions, you may email hrquestions@roosevelt.edu . Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Required Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, Human Resources, or a related field required. Minimum of two to three years of progressively responsible payroll experience required, including full-cycle payroll processing. Experience processing multiple payroll cycles in a complex organizational environment. ·        Demonstrated knowledge of federal, state, and local payroll tax regulations, wage and hour laws, payroll compliance requirements, institutional policies, and collective bargaining agreements, as applicable. Working knowledge of payroll systems, HRIS platforms, and time and attendance systems required. ·Experience with payroll tax filings, W-2 preparation, garnishments, payroll reconciliations, and related payroll reporting. Understanding of payroll accounting principles, including general ledger reconciliations and journal entry preparation. Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Excel, including data analysis, reconciliation, and reporting; working knowledge of Word and Outlook required. Ability to manage and improve payroll processes, controls, and procedures while supporting accuracy, compliance, and continuous improvement. Ability to lead payroll audits, prepare compliance documentation, maintain audit-ready records, and respond to internal and external audit requests. Ability to research, analyze, and resolve payroll discrepancies and employee inquiries. Ability to train, mentor, or provide guidance to payroll staff. Strong analytical, organizational, project management, verbal, and written communication skills, with the ability to manage competing deadlines and explain payroll concepts clearly. · Ability to exercise sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, and handle sensitive information with discretion. Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with Human Resources, Finance, Financial Aid, and academic and administrative departments. Strong commitment to accuracy, compliance, continuous improvement, customer service, and Roosevelt’s core values, mission, and vision. Years of Experience Required 2-3 Required Education Bachelor's Degree Certification/Licensure Required Minimum Qualifications Please refer to knowledge, skills, and abilities required. Preferred Qualifications Experience processing payroll in a higher education, nonprofit, union, or multi-payroll environment. Experience with ADP Workforce Now and Ellucian Banner. Prior experience supervising or leading payroll, administrative, or shared services staff. Experience with student employment payroll, Federal Work-Study reconciliation, restricted fund reconciliation, general ledger reconciliation, or payroll-related journal entries. Experience supporting year-end payroll activities, audit responses, and compliance documentation. Certified Payroll Professional ( CPP ) or Fundamental Payroll Certification ( FPC ) certification. Equipment Operated Basic office equipment (desktop computer, copier/multi-function device, printer, fax and telephone). Working Conditions Normal climate-controlled office environment is provided. Job is largely sedentary, but there may be a need to move about the office frequently. Occasional bending, stooping, lifting, pushing and/or pulling is required (typically less than 10 pounds of weight or pressure). Regular use of desktop computer is required, calling for frequent hand/wrist movement and repetition. Priority Application Instructions Departmental Contact Information Essential Job Functions Duty and Responsibility Process accurate and timely payroll by reviewing and validating payroll data, correcting discrepancies, processing off-cycle and manual payments, and supporting W-2, year-end, audit, record retention, and internal control activities. Provide oversight to the Payroll Administrator, respond to payroll questions, communicate payroll policies, process stop/reverse/void payments in ADP , and reconcile payroll funds with the Business Office and Federal Work-Study payroll amounts with Financial Aid. Percentage Of Time 50 Duty and Responsibility Prepare biweekly and monthly payroll data, checks, bank payment files, and federal and state tax files. Review Banner and ADP discrepancies before payroll approval and maintain payroll records, reports, compliance documentation, and reconciliation support. Percentage Of Time 20 Duty and Responsibility Research and resolve employee payroll questions and concerns. Partner with Human Resources, Benefits, Finance, Financial Aid, and departments to support accurate payroll processing, funding reconciliation, compliance, and employee service. Percentage Of Time 20 Duty and Responsibility Administer ADP Time & Attendance, process payroll redistributions, supervise the Payroll Administrator, provide training and performance support, and prepare required payroll reports on schedule. Percentage Of Time 10 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have experience preparing account analysis and reconciliations? Yes No * Do you have a Bachelor's Degree in a relevant field? Yes No * Do you have previous experience working in Ellucian/ Banner? Yes No Do you have payroll processing experience using ADP? Yes No This is a hybrid position. Do you have the ability to work on the Chicago campus 3 days per week and attend any other in-person events as required? Yes No Will you now or at any point in the future require employment visa sponsorship (e.g., H-1B) to legally work in the United States? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents 430 S. Michigan, Chicago, IL To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
